WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.800
Procurement Intelligence Lab turns conflicting documents into a reviewable, evidence-backed decision.

00:03.800 --> 00:07.600
Reviewers compare governed requirements with observed records while provenance remains visible.

00:07.600 --> 00:11.400
Evidence, deterministic state, and human decision authority remain separate.

00:11.400 --> 00:15.200
Two eligible approved requirements disagree; the correct value is unresolved, not zero.

00:15.200 --> 00:19.000
The system captures, structures, compares, abstains, and presents one cited finding for review.

00:19.000 --> 00:22.800
Procurement scenarios include quantity, missing-data, revision, price, timing, and recovery checks.

00:22.800 --> 00:26.600
Other domains are architecture candidates only; procurement is the implemented vertical.

00:26.600 --> 00:30.400
Now follow one conflict from question to original evidence and human disposition.

00:30.400 --> 00:35.500
The operator types a bounded item and cutoff character by character. This is current-build fixture execution with no model call.

00:35.500 --> 00:40.500
Each cited source opens in context and highlights the cells that support the finding.

00:40.500 --> 00:43.000
The unresolved finding is rejected. The disposition is retained without rewriting the source conflict or placing an order.
